iar about all this speaking of  familiar and taken from stuff there were  a few scenes in here that  i had seen in other mcu movies not just  oh seen it in another movie before i've  seen this in the mcu before like someone  does the loki trick they do the loki i  was something happens in here where i  was like that's loki's move by the way  i've seen loki do it and you just did it  again it doesn't feel like that oh but  it's all interconnected and it's the  same universe and these are super old  characters and maybe they taught loki  how to do it rest assured they're gonna  say that that's the case they're gonna  say like no loki learned that move from  this character  like that kid in iron man 2 is peter  parker that's called a retcon it's not  just that one scene there were a few  scenes in here i was like i've seen that  in the mcu before just felt very  familiar like i said earlier in this  video it's like the movie feels  different enough it's like someone got  freaked out and had to remind everyone  like oh yeah it's an mcu movie do some  really mcuish things but in the end the  movie was reliably entertaining as  generally speaking the mcu is it has a  good message about humanity having faith  in people what human beings are capable  of and how human beings at their worst  isn't really what humanity has to offer  i appreciate stuff like that the concept  of eternals is a lot more interesting  than the execution of eternals i think  this movie and what i saw could have  been  a masterpiece of sorts especially among  the mcu but the movie seems so afraid to  go its own direction and commit to its  high concept that it kind of dabbles its  toe into a couple times it springs back  to the mcu safe zone on more than a few  occasions and it leaves you going all  right i was still entertained no alcohol  required but this movie could have been  so much more alright so eternals have  you seen it what did you think about it  i know it's a bit early but eventually  th